================================================================================
  DATASET — indian_insurance_dataset.csv
================================================================================

Located at the workspace root. This is the raw training data used to build
the premium prediction ML model (insurance_premium_model.pkl).

  Contains records of Indian insurance policyholders with columns:
    age, sex, bmi, children, smoker, disease, policy_type, premium (target)

  The model was trained offline on this dataset using XGBoost regression
  and serialised with joblib. The CSV is not used at runtime — only the
  trained .pkl model is loaded by the server.

================================================================================
  Insurance-AI/ — REFERENCE COPY
================================================================================

A nested Git repository (has its own .git/ folder) containing an earlier or
reference copy of the frontend code. Its structure is identical to frontend/:
same Vite + React + TypeScript setup, same package.json, same src/ files.

This appears to be the original repository that was cloned into the workspace.
It does NOT contain a backend. It is not actively used in the current project —
the working frontend is in the top-level frontend/ directory.

================================================================================
  HOW THE RAG PIPELINE WORKS (end to end)
================================================================================

  BUILD TIME (run once with vector_store.py):
    JSON files in insurance_rag_data/
      -> load_documents.py converts each entry to a LangChain Document
      -> RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter splits into ~400 char chunks
      -> HuggingFace all-MiniLM-L6-v2 converts each chunk to a 384-dim vector
      -> FAISS indexes all vectors and saves to insurance_faiss_db/

  RUNTIME (every /chat request):
    User types question in browser
      -> axios POST to http://127.0.0.1:8000/chat
      -> FastAPI receives { question }
      -> FAISS similarity_search finds top 3 most relevant chunks
      -> Chunks joined into context string
      -> Prompt built: "You are an expert Indian health insurance assistant..."
      -> ChatMistralAI sends prompt to Mistral cloud (open-mistral-7b)
      -> LLM generates answer using context
      -> clean_response() strips markdown formatting
      -> { answer } returned to frontend
      -> React appends bot message to chatLog

================================================================================
  HOW THE PREMIUM PREDICTION WORKS (end to end)
================================================================================

  BUILD TIME (offline, not in this repo):
    indian_insurance_dataset.csv
      -> Feature engineering and encoding
      -> XGBoost regressor trained (300 trees)
      -> Model saved as insurance_premium_model.pkl and .json

  RUNTIME (every /predict request):
    User fills form and clicks "Calculate Premium"
      -> axios POST to http://127.0.0.1:8000/predict with 7 fields
      -> FastAPI validates with PredictRequest Pydantic model
      -> Fields wrapped in pandas DataFrame (single row)
      -> joblib-loaded XGBoost model runs inference
      -> Predicted premium (float) cast to int
      -> { premium: 18500 } returned to frontend
      -> React displays ₹18,500 in the result banner

================================================================================
  API REFERENCE
================================================================================

  Base URL: http://127.0.0.1:8000

  GET /
  Response: { "status": "Insurance RAG + Premium Prediction API Running" }

  POST /chat
  Request:  { "question": "What is a waiting period?" }
  Response: { "answer": "A waiting period is the initial time during which..." }

  POST /predict
  Request:
    {
      "age": 35,
      "sex": 1,
      "bmi": 26.5,
      "children": 2,
      "smoker": 0,
      "disease": 5,
      "policy_type": 1
    }
  Response: { "premium": 18500 }

  Field encodings:
    sex:         1=Male, 0=Female
    smoker:      1=Smoker, 0=Non-Smoker
    disease:     0=Asthma, 1=Diabetes, 2=Heart Disease,
                 3=Hypertension, 4=Multiple Conditions, 5=None
    policy_type: 0=Family Floater, 1=Individual, 2=Senior Citizen

================================================================================
  SETUP AND RUNNING
================================================================================

  PREREQUISITES
    - Python 3.10+ with pip
    - Node.js 18+ with npm
    - Mistral AI API key (get from https://console.mistral.ai/)

  BACKEND SETUP

    cd backend

    # Create virtual environment
    python -m venv venv

    # Activate it
    venv\Scripts\activate          (Windows CMD)
    venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1      (Windows PowerShell)
    source venv/bin/activate       (Linux/Mac)

    # Install all dependencies
    pip install -r requirements.txt

    # Add your Mistral API key to .env
    # Edit backend/.env and set:
    # MISTRAL_API_KEY=your_actual_key_here

    # Build the FAISS vector database (ONE TIME ONLY)
    python vector_store.py
    # You should see: "Vector database created and saved."

    # Start the API server
    uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
    # Server runs at http://127.0.0.1:8000

  FRONTEND SETUP

    cd frontend

    # Install dependencies
    npm install

    # Start development server
    npm run dev
    # App opens at http://localhost:5173

    # Build for production
    npm run build
    # Output goes to frontend/dist/

  RUNNING BOTH TOGETHER
    Open two terminals:
      Terminal 1: cd backend && uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
      Terminal 2: cd frontend && npm run dev
    Then open http://localhost:5173 in your browser.

================================================================================
  IMPORTANT NOTES
================================================================================

  1. The .env file contains a real API key. Do not commit it to git.
     The backend/.gitignore already excludes it.

  2. The .pkl and .faiss files are also in .gitignore. If you clone this
     project fresh, you need to:
       a) Obtain or retrain insurance_premium_model.pkl
       b) Run python vector_store.py to rebuild the FAISS index

  3. The FAISS index uses allow_dangerous_deserialization=True because
     the index.pkl was created locally. Only load indexes you built yourself.

  4. The Mistral AI LLM call requires an internet connection and a valid
     API key. The embedding model (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) runs fully locally
     and downloads automatically on first use via HuggingFace Hub.

  5. The React Compiler (babel-plugin-react-compiler) is experimental.
     If you encounter build issues, you can remove it from vite.config.ts
     and the package.json devDependencies.

